[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Edgemodders/REDnode/main/packs/ui-tools/nexus/brand/banner.png[/img][/center]

[center][size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]Read Night City's own UI. Pick any widget. Build native UI of your own.[/color][/b][/size][/center]

[center][size=3]REDnode UI Tools is an app pack for UI modders. Its UI Workbench shows the game's own interface, the ink widgets the engine draws, as a live tree: point at any piece of the HUD or a menu and it tells you what it is, where it came from and every property it has. Then write native UI of your own in ink markup, HTML-style tags the game draws as its own.[/size][/center]

[line]

[quote][size=4][b][color=#fcee0a]STATUS: PREVIEW[/color][/b][/size]
Built in the open and tested in the game on game version 2.5. It runs on [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/35419]REDnode[/url] and [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/7780]Codeware[/url], which you need first. Everything it does reads the game's UI; nothing it shows changes the game.
[b]UI modders:[/b] this is for you. [b]Players:[/b] you do not need it to play UI mods.[/quote][line]

[i][color=#19f3ff]Screenshot 1: the UI Workbench over the HUD, a widget picked and outlined, its details on the right[/color][/i]

[size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]What is in the pack[/color][/b][/size]

[size=4][b][color=#19f3ff]UI Workbench: Inspect[/color][/b][/size]
Every ink layer of the game as a tree: the HUD with each of its pieces (the health bar, the minimap, the quest tracker...), the menus, notifications. Open any widget to see its children.
[list]
[*][b]Pick:[/b] point at the HUD or a menu. The widget under the cursor is outlined and named as you move; click it, and the tree opens down to it with its row selected. Only what the game draws is offered, the smallest widget under the cursor first.[/*]
[*][b]Right-click while picking[/b] sets the widget on top aside, so the one under it can be picked.[/*]
[*][b]Pick inside:[/b] with a widget selected, pick only among its children.[/*]
[*][b]Details:[/b] a widget's class, path, box on screen, controllers, the .inkwidget file it was spawned from, and every property, each part folding away. Copy its path or all of it as JSON.[/*]
[*][b]Filter[/b] the tree by name, class, controller or text.[/*]
[*]HUD pieces the game has not spawned yet (a boss health bar, a car's HUD) are listed and say so.[/*]
[/list][i][color=#19f3ff]Screenshot 2: Pick in a menu, with the tree opened to the widget[/color][/i]

[size=4][b][color=#19f3ff]UI Workbench: Edit[/color][/b][/size]
[i][color=#19f3ff]To be written with phase UT3: the editor (markup and script, Run and Stop, To source from a picked panel, projects and Export).[/color][/i]

[i][color=#19f3ff]Screenshot 3: the editor with a panel of ink markup running on the HUD[/color][/i]

[size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]Requirements[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/35419]REDnode[/url] 0.53.7 or later, with what it needs (RED4ext, redscript).[/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/7780]Codeware[/url] 1.16 or later.[/*]
[*]Cyberpunk 2077 on PC, game version 2.5.[/*]
[/list][size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]Install[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Vortex:[/b] Mod Manager Download, then enable and deploy.[/*]
[*][b]By hand:[/b] extract the zip into the game folder, so the app lands in [i]red4ext/plugins/REDnode/apps/[/i].[/*]
[/list]In the game, press [b]F10[/b] and open the [b]Mod Manager[/b] from the launcher (the [b]REDNODE[/b] tab at the lower left). Switch on the [b]UI Workbench[/b]; it starts switched off and asks for no permission.

[b]Uninstall:[/b] remove it in your mod manager, or delete the [i]ui-workbench[/i] folder from [i]red4ext/plugins/REDnode/apps/[/i]. REDnode itself stays.

[size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]For mod makers[/color][/b][/size]

Everything the Workbench reads is in REDnode's [b]rednode[/b] package, for your own mods: [i]ink.layers[/i] for the game's layers and HUD pieces, [i]ink.read[/i] for a tree of widgets in one call, [i]ink.inspect[/i] for one widget in full, [i]ink.at[/i] and [i]ink.boxes[/i] for what is under a point. Native UI of your own is written with [i]ink.load[/i] and [i]ink.parse[/i] in ink markup, or with the [i]ink[/i] functions. See the [url=https://edgemodders.github.io/REDnode/ink.html]native UI docs[/url].

[size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]Questions[/color][/b][/size]

[b]Does it slow the game down?[/b]
A pick reads about 450 widgets in under 3 ms. While Pick is on, the boxes are read again every 1.5 s; moving the mouse asks the game nothing.

[b]Why can I not click a HUD piece in the tree?[/b]
The game makes many HUD pieces only when they are needed (a video, a boss fight, a vehicle). Until then there is nothing to show; select it again after Refresh once it is on screen.

[b]Is it free?[/b]
Yes, and open source under the MIT license, in [url=https://github.com/Edgemodders/REDnode]REDnode's repo[/url].

